hi i'm jenny and today i'd like to show  you how to use the apogee adapter for  envoy together with a service mesh  to integrate envoy based services into  your apogee environment  in this demo i'll show you how to use  envoy to protect a microservice  i'll add an envoy facade on it which is  configured to talk to the apogee adapter  for envoy  let's dive in i have a kubernetes  cluster that has a few applications  running the one we'll focus on for this  demo is the microservice called orders  by default there is no restriction on  who can access this microservice  let me demonstrate that by accessing it  as a consumer  to simulate a consumer i have a curl  application running in client  once i am logged into the client  application i will access the orders  microservice  based on this result i was able to  access it without passing through any  security credentials  now let me walk you through how you can  enforce the security policy so that a  consumer  must use credentials within a service  mesh to do that  i'll enable an envoy filter  i've created a file that describes all  the security policies i want to enforce  on the orders microservice  for instance i'm enforcing a policy that  requests must go through the apogee  adapter  i'm now applying this policy via the  filter  now i'm going to access the orders  microservice again  like i did before  this time i got an error a 403 forbidden  because i didn't have a security  credential let's fix that  we'll do this through the api products  in apogee  i've already created an orders api  product which is bound to the endpoint  orders running on port 8080  i've also created an application that  allows me to access the credentials for  the orders microservice  let's access the orders microservice  again this time with the api key  i'm using an api key but you could also  use an access token instead  success i was able to access the  microservice  through all these interactions analytics  are being collected and transmitted to  the apigee control panel  looking at the api metrics here you'll  notice that the orders microservice is  getting requests and i can view the data  for that  this is how you can use the apogee  adapter for envoy to enforce policies  for any service that's using envoy  within a service  mesh if you found this demo helpful  check out our introductory apogee  adapter for envoy video  linked in the description below and for  more information like codelabs and blog  posts  check out these links thanks for  [Music]  watching
 

